<h1>Hot Lab for Department WCMs - October 29, 2026</h1>
<div class="meta-row">
<div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Type</span><span class="meta-value"><span class="doc-type-badge">Meeting Record</span></span></div>
<div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Playbook</span><span class="meta-value">Department WCM Hot Lab</span></div>
<div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Date</span><span class="meta-value">October 29, 2026</span></div>
<div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Series</span><span class="meta-value">Recurring, Tuesdays and Thursdays</span></div>
<div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Platform</span><span class="meta-value">Microsoft Teams</span></div>
<div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Attendees</span><span class="meta-value">7 named in the transcript</span></div>
<div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Version</span><span class="meta-value">1.0</span></div>
</div>
<div class="audience-banner"><p><strong>Audience:</strong> Department Web Content Managers and the District Web Team. Led by Sean A. Russell. A support session the day before the certification deadline: audit pages that belong to another office, how the two-column check is read, out-of-date content, a tooltip request, and what happens after the deadline.</p></div>
<nav aria-label="On this page" class="page-index"><p class="pi-label">On this page</p><ol><li><a href="#g1">The Meeting</a><span class="pi-count">1 section</span></li><li><a href="#g2">What We Decided</a><span class="pi-count">2 sections</span></li><li><a href="#g3">Your To-Do List</a><span class="pi-count">2 sections</span></li><li><a href="#g4">Resources and History</a><span class="pi-count">1 section</span></li></ol></nav>
<h2 class="lead-heading">Summary</h2>
<div class="section-block lead-summary">
<p class="gap-note" style="margin:0 0 12px">The recording link will be added here once it is posted from Teams.</p>
<p><strong>Certification is due tomorrow, October 30.</strong> Most WCMs are making it through, and the issues raised so far were fixed for everyone. Access will not be cut off Friday evening: the course stays open through the weekend, and at the end of the day Monday, November 2, the District Web Team checks who has not finished. WCMs who are close (95% or more) get a personal follow-up; WCMs who have not started or are far from done get a separate message with next steps. If something is stopping you from reaching 100%, message Sean on Teams today.</p>
<p><strong>Audit pages that belong to another office.</strong> Jennifer N. Amador found two pages in the Early Childhood Education audit that her team does not manage: <em>Welcome to Kindergarten</em> belongs to Elementary Education (Jamie Ferguson), and <em>Employee Early Childhood Education Opportunities</em> is not Head Start or VPK, so its owner still has to be found. Because some departments look like one office from the outside, every WCM is asked to check that their audit lists only the pages their team manages, and to flag any that are not theirs.</p>
<p><strong>The two-column check.</strong> The single-column standard is about the page layout (a whole page split into left and right columns, as many pages were brought over from SchoolWires). A small section that sits side by side, such as an Important Links block or a logo beside the intro paragraph, is fine. The audit currently flags those too; that is being corrected, so skip that item for now and it will be re-run next week.</p>
<p><strong>Dates and information are current.</strong> When a page shows past school years, review it with your team. Often it is a chance to post an update, even a short one. If your team decides the wording should stay as it is, say so in the note on the item.</p>
<p><strong>Tell your department''s story.</strong> The District is shifting from making sure websites are correct to helping departments tell their story: videos, spotlights and an editorial calendar of the events that happen every year, so content can be planned and reused. More guidance will follow, including at the quarterly meeting.</p>
<p><strong>Still stuck? on an audit item</strong> is the way to ask. Give as much detail as you can. Questions are answered in the order received, and when several people ask about the same thing it moves up the list. Items that belong to Finalsite (such as PDF tagging rules and template markup) are being filtered out of WCM lists again.</p>
</div>
<section aria-labelledby="g1" class="doc-group"><h2 class="eyebrow" id="g1">The Meeting</h2><p class="group-note">Who was there and what was covered.</p>
<details class="doc-accordion"><summary><h3>Who Attended</h3></summary><div class="section-block"><div class="attendee-grid">
<div class="attendee-card"><div class="attendee-name">Sean A. Russell</div><div class="attendee-title">District Webmaster, Office of Communications</div></div>
<div class="attendee-card"><div class="attendee-name">Jennifer Amador</div><div class="attendee-title">Early Childhood Education</div></div>
<div class="attendee-card"><div class="attendee-name">Lilia E. Durham</div><div class="attendee-title">Safety &amp; Security Operations</div></div>
<div class="attendee-card"><div class="attendee-name">Vince Watson</div><div class="attendee-title">School Culture &amp; Student Support</div></div>
<div class="attendee-card"><div class="attendee-name">Marcia Dixon</div><div class="attendee-title">EEO / ADA Compliance</div></div>
<div class="attendee-card"><div class="attendee-name">Patricia Sapp</div><div class="attendee-title">Labor Relations</div></div>
<div class="attendee-card"><div class="attendee-name">Jhonii Louis</div><div class="attendee-title">Student Services &amp; Mental Health</div></div>
</div><p class="gap-note">Names from the Teams transcript. Others who joined without speaking are not listed.</p></div></details>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="g2" class="doc-group"><h2 class="eyebrow" id="g2">What We Decided</h2><p class="group-note">Decisions made in the meeting and questions still open.</p>
<details class="doc-accordion" open><summary><h3>Decisions</h3></summary><div class="section-block">
<div class="highlight-row"><div class="hl-label">Confirmed</div><div class="hl-text"><strong>Certification grace period.</strong> The course stays open through the weekend. The check of who has not finished happens at the end of the day Monday, November 2.</div></div>
<div class="highlight-row"><div class="hl-label">Confirmed</div><div class="hl-text"><strong>Two-column means the page layout.</strong> Side-by-side sections such as Important Links or a logo beside the intro are allowed. The audit will be adjusted so it stops flagging them.</div></div>
<div class="highlight-row"><div class="hl-label">Confirmed</div><div class="hl-text"><strong>Out-of-date content is a team decision.</strong> Review the page with your team; update it, or note that you reviewed it and are keeping the wording.</div></div>
<div class="highlight-row"><div class="hl-label">Confirmed</div><div class="hl-text"><strong>Questions go through Still stuck?</strong> on the audit item, with as much detail as possible. Repeated questions move up the list.</div></div>
<div class="highlight-row"><div class="hl-label">Confirmed</div><div class="hl-text"><strong>Welcome to Kindergarten</strong> belongs to Elementary Education, not Early Childhood Education.</div></div>
</div></details>
<details class="doc-accordion"><summary><h3>Open Questions</h3></summary><div class="section-block">
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Who manages Employee Early Childhood Education Opportunities?</div><div class="point-detail">Not Head Start or VPK. Sean thought it may belong to another office; the District Web Team is researching it.</div></div>
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Hover tooltips for a training list</div><div class="point-detail">Vince Watson was asked for a page where hovering over a training shows its description. The District Web Team checks whether Finalsite does this natively; if not, it can be built as a widget. Vince will build what he can with current tools first.</div></div>
</div></details>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="g3" class="doc-group"><h2 class="eyebrow" id="g3">Your To-Do List</h2><p class="group-note">Who does what next.</p>
<details class="doc-accordion" open><summary><h3>Action Items</h3></summary><div class="section-block">
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">1</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Finish certification</div><div class="action-detail">Message Sean on Teams today if anything is stopping you from reaching 100%.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: Department WCMs who have not finished</div><div class="action-deadline">October 30</div></div></div>
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">2</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Check your audit lists only your pages</div><div class="action-detail">Flag any page that belongs to another office with Still stuck? or by selecting it for reclassification.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: Department WCMs</div></div></div>
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">3</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Move the Early Childhood Education pages that are not theirs</div><div class="action-detail">Welcome to Kindergarten to Elementary Education. Find the owner of Employee Early Childhood Education Opportunities.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: District Web Team</div></div></div>
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">4</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Early Childhood Education widget</div><div class="action-detail">Lindsey Way sent the spreadsheet; build the draft and share it with Lindsey Way and Jennifer Amador.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: Sean A. Russell</div></div></div>
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">5</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Adjust the single-column check</div><div class="action-detail">Find pages flagged for side-by-side columns, confirm with Sean which are acceptable (such as Important Links), update the check, and re-run next week.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: District Web Team</div><div class="action-deadline">Next week</div></div></div>
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">6</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Review the Metal Detector Program page</div><div class="action-detail">Talk with your team about an update, or note that the wording stays.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: Lilia E. Durham</div></div></div>
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">7</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Tooltip request</div><div class="action-detail">Build it with current tools first. If the requester needs more, bring an example and book 30 minutes with Sean through his scheduling link.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: Vince Watson</div></div></div>
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">8</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Fix the double header on the dashboard</div><div class="action-detail">Patricia Sapp saw two department headers after the Dashboard button change.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: District Web Team</div></div></div>
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">9</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Keep Finalsite''s items off WCM lists</div><div class="action-detail">PDF and template rules that only Finalsite can fix are showing on WCM lists again. Filter them out and finish the Audit Error Guide review.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: District Web Team</div></div></div>
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">10</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Answer the audit questions</div><div class="action-detail">Questions sent with Still stuck? are answered in order; a reminder is set so none wait long.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: Sean A. Russell</div></div></div>
<div class="action-item"><div class="action-num">11</div><div class="action-body"><div class="action-title">Email update to all WCMs</div><div class="action-detail">Sent from Outlook while the District grants access for the automatic weekly email.</div><div class="action-owner">Owner: Sean A. Russell</div><div class="action-deadline">October 29</div></div></div>
</div></details>
<details class="doc-accordion"><summary><h3>Next Steps</h3></summary><div class="section-block">
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">October 30</div><div class="point-detail">Department WCM certification deadline.</div></div>
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Monday, November 2</div><div class="point-detail">End-of-day check of who has not finished certification.</div></div>
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Next Hot Lab</div><div class="point-detail">Tuesday, November 3.</div></div>
