<h1>District Web Team Huddle - October 28, 2026</h1>
<div class="meta-row">
<div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Type</span><span class="meta-value"><span class="doc-type-badge">Meeting Record</span></span></div>
<div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Playbook</span><span class="meta-value">District Web Team Tools</span></div>
<div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Date</span><span class="meta-value">October 28, 2026</span></div>
<div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Series</span><span class="meta-value">Weekly, Wednesdays</span></div>
<div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Platform</span><span class="meta-value">Microsoft Teams</span></div>
<div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Attendees</span><span class="meta-value">7 named in the transcript</span></div>
<div class="meta-item"><span class="meta-label">Version</span><span class="meta-value">1.0</span></div>
</div>
<div class="audience-banner"><p><strong>Audience:</strong> the District Web Team. A walk through the Web Team Assignments tracker. Each update is credited to the person who gave it; the tracker rows were updated and consolidated from these notes the same day.</p></div>
<nav aria-label="On this page" class="page-index"><p class="pi-label">On this page</p><ol><li><a href="#g1">The Meeting</a><span class="pi-count">2 sections</span></li><li><a href="#g2">What We Decided</a><span class="pi-count">1 section</span></li><li><a href="#g3">Your To-Do List</a><span class="pi-count">1 section</span></li><li><a href="#g4">Resources and History</a><span class="pi-count">1 section</span></li></ol></nav>
<h2 class="lead-heading">Summary</h2>
<div class="section-block lead-summary">
<p><strong>Pilot schools.</strong> Instead of rolling the school ADA scan, audit and submission tools out to every school at once, each school lead picks about three responsive schools to test them first. The Banner Submission pilot folds into the same group. Vanessa C. Deslandes''s team is building one spreadsheet of school page links (homepage, School Choice and magnet landing pages) together with the BCPS Central certification data, so school profiles fill from one source.</p>
<p><strong>The tracker gets shorter.</strong> Duplicates were merged and finished rows archived. Before each huddle, everyone reviews their rows and adds updates with Add your input (typed or recorded), so the meeting can focus on decisions. Tracker notes are credited to the person who gave the update.</p>
<p><strong>New work:</strong> an inventory of department content shared on school websites (Felicia C. Hicks and Andrea Barton, with Vanessa), a look at smaller heading sizes, deadline reminders 48 hours ahead, and looping Tricia A. Allen into the AI website platform conversation.</p>
</div>
<section aria-labelledby="g1" class="doc-group"><h2 class="eyebrow" id="g1">The Meeting</h2><p class="group-note">Who was there and the updates, by person.</p>
<details class="doc-accordion"><summary><h3>Who Attended</h3></summary><div class="section-block"><div class="attendee-grid">
<div class="attendee-card"><div class="attendee-name">Sean A. Russell</div><div class="attendee-title">District Webmaster, Office of Communications</div></div>
<div class="attendee-card"><div class="attendee-name">Vanessa C. Deslandes</div><div class="attendee-title">District Web Team</div></div>
<div class="attendee-card"><div class="attendee-name">Felicia C. Hicks</div><div class="attendee-title">Webmaster 1, Office of Communications</div></div>
<div class="attendee-card"><div class="attendee-name">Tricia A. Allen</div><div class="attendee-title">District Web Team</div></div>
<div class="attendee-card"><div class="attendee-name">Rodolfo M. Carril</div><div class="attendee-title">District Web Team</div></div>
<div class="attendee-card"><div class="attendee-name">Andrea Barton</div><div class="attendee-title">District Web Team</div></div>
<div class="attendee-card"><div class="attendee-name">Nakesha Ali-Sirju</div><div class="attendee-title">District Web Team</div></div>
</div><p class="gap-note">Names from the Teams transcript. Titles other than Sean''s and Felicia''s are not in the WCM records; confirm.</p></div></details>
<details class="doc-accordion" open><summary><h3>Updates by Person</h3></summary><div class="section-block">
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Vanessa C. Deslandes</div><div class="point-detail"><strong>School audits 2026-27:</strong> responses are coming in as WCMs finish the course and get access. The school audit is due December 1 and the media center update December 18. Submission numbers come to the next huddle (with Nakesha Ali-Sirju). <strong>School data sheet:</strong> she will export the BCPS Central list and add page links; the team meets this afternoon to pick at least three sites each. <strong>Banner Submission:</strong> large uploads are now compressed automatically; she will review it once more. Only two or three of the seven pilot WCMs gave feedback. <strong>WCM directory:</strong> WCMs got introduction emails and the Communique; the next Communique will remind them to look up their web lead in the directory. <strong>Path to Certification graphic:</strong> a draft exists with Tricia; she aims to finish by October 30. <strong>Governance document:</strong> she has the link and will review it. <strong>WCM Guidelines:</strong> shared; the athletics section is paused. She sends a follow-up to the director and Ms. Jaylin today; target November 13. <strong>BCPS Central:</strong> Yaco has the dashboard requests and said he made updates; she will check what changed. <strong>Athletics template:</strong> waiting on the department about how student information can be shown (FERPA). <strong>Portals:</strong> asked for a school version of the parent portal for the Parents &amp; Families landing page (phase two), and noted LineWise can be a reused page; she is waiting for the ticket. <strong>WCM Communique:</strong> the next one goes out the week of November 9. <strong>New:</strong> proposed an inventory of department content shared on school sites, starting from the elementary, middle and high standards in the Community Hub. Asked for deadline reminders 48 hours ahead and how the team adds updates.</div></div>
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Tricia A. Allen</div><div class="point-detail">Will follow up with Dr. Fleming on the date of the principals meeting this week, since the certification graphic may be needed sooner. Athletics: send Patty Brown''s team a priority email marked as a second or third attempt with a deadline; if there is no reply, move ahead (Farrah as backup on FERPA, or remove that content). Breakout rooms: the organizer can pre-assign people to rooms during the opening segment. Suggested everyone review the tracker before the meeting and submit updates in advance. Agreed to be looped into the AI website platform conversation because she oversees the RFP.</div></div>
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Rodolfo M. Carril</div><div class="point-detail">Confirmed the BCPS Central meeting with Yaco was last week. School Hot Labs: about 15 people at the busiest point yesterday; Tuesdays focus on WCMs still in the course, Thursdays are open. Many school WCMs say they will finish the course when they have time.</div></div>
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Felicia C. Hicks</div><div class="point-detail">Referendum button and pop-up stay up through November 3, with no changes. Will co-lead the shared content inventory with Andrea Barton. Asked for a way to leave a standing note on rows that will not change.</div></div>
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Andrea Barton</div><div class="point-detail">Updates the certified list in the SharePoint master list weekly; sending Sean the link. Volunteered for the shared content inventory; meeting Vanessa to get started.</div></div>
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Sean A. Russell</div><div class="point-detail"><strong>ADA scanner:</strong> ready; running it on pilot schools first, then the audit scan for schools, alongside the migration plan. <strong>Portal refresh:</strong> parent portal prototype built in BCPS MarComm and shared with Farrah; one more round, then the template for students and community, plus a quarterly check-in with departments that own sections. On hold while the newsroom project runs; Finalsite cannot create new newsroom categories (they are looking into it). <strong>School WCM certification assessment</strong> folds into the website governance work. <strong>Department roster:</strong> deadline Friday; removals November 2; extensions case by case; email to WCMs this afternoon; directors invited to the platform. <strong>Department audits:</strong> running and in use; a guide is still needed. The Audit Error Guide is for the whole team to review, since schools will use the same system. <strong>Headings:</strong> proposed smaller heading sizes (for example H1 from 22 to 20, H2 from 18 to 16) so WCMs stop skipping levels for size. <strong>Platform plan:</strong> presenting the migration plan to Tricia, Manny and Farrah. <strong>AI for the website platform:</strong> a request to talk about AI for the website platform came in after the last meeting; looping in Tricia. <strong>AI liaisons</strong> move under website governance. <strong>Market Your School workshop:</strong> adding a short certification course; framework to share by November 13. <strong>Graphics workflow:</strong> waiting on Michael for a date. <strong>Magnet widget:</strong> map, program search, a seasonal School Choice menu, school logos from Graphics. <strong>Video strategy:</strong> target 2027. <strong>About Us:</strong> the history saved from the old site, after portals. <strong>PMO:</strong> Ernesto Gonzalez will update the LineWise page. <strong>Countdown widget:</strong> marketing was not sure it adds much; the real question is what Magnet is trying to achieve.</div></div>
<div class="point-item"><div class="point-title">Nakesha Ali-Sirju</div><div class="point-detail">Joined from the office; Vanessa gave the audit update.</div></div>
</div></details>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="g2" class="doc-group"><h2 class="eyebrow" id="g2">What We Decided</h2><p class="group-note">Decisions made in the meeting.</p>
<details class="doc-accordion" open><summary><h3>Decisions</h3></summary><div class="section-block">
<div class="highlight-row"><div class="hl-label">Confirmed</div><div class="hl-text"><strong>Pilot schools.</strong> Each school lead picks about three schools to test new tools first; the banner pilot joins this group.</div></div>
<div class="highlight-row"><div class="hl-label">Confirmed</div><div class="hl-text"><strong>One school data sheet.</strong> Page links and BCPS Central data in one spreadsheet that fills school profiles; the SharePoint school logos item folds in.</div></div>
<div class="highlight-row"><div class="hl-label">Confirmed</div><div class="hl-text"><strong>Website governance absorbs</strong> the school WCM certification assessment, the internal web steering committee and AI liaisons.</div></div>
<div class="highlight-row"><div class="hl-label">Confirmed</div><div class="hl-text"><strong>Quarterly meeting breakouts</strong> by school lead, with rooms pre-assigned by a second organizer.</div></div>
<div class="highlight-row"><div class="hl-label">Confirmed</div><div class="hl-text"><strong>One weekly huddle.</strong> Everyone reviews the tracker beforehand and adds updates with Add your input; the tracker is consolidated so the review is shorter.</div></div>
<div class="highlight-row"><div class="hl-label">Confirmed</div><div class="hl-text"><strong>Shared content inventory</strong> led by Felicia C. Hicks and Andrea Barton, with Vanessa C. Deslandes.</div></div>
</div></details>
</section>
