 replace(replace(replace(replace(replace(regexp_replace(content, '<p><strong>Status\.</strong>.*?</p>', '<p><strong>Status.</strong> Certification is due <strong>Friday, October 30, 2026</strong>. As of October 29, 45 department WCMs have completed it. The course stays open through the weekend; <strong>at the end of the day Monday, November 2, the District Web Team checks who has not finished, and access to edit your department website is paused until you complete it.</strong> If something is stopping you from reaching 100%, message Sean on Teams now. The department audit is live on your dashboard under <strong>Run Audit</strong>; first, check that it lists only pages your team manages (see Your Department Audit below).</p>'),
 '<span class="meta-label">Last Updated</span><span class="meta-value">October 28, 2026</span>', '<span class="meta-label">Last Updated</span><span class="meta-value">October 29, 2026</span>'),
 '<p>The most common red item so far is <strong>Quick Access buttons</strong>', '<p><strong>Updated October 29:</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Check that your audit lists only your pages.</strong> Some departments look like one office from the outside, so we rely on you. If a page belongs to another office, select it for reclassification, or use Still stuck? and tell us who manages it.</li>
<li><strong>Side-by-side sections are allowed.</strong> The single-column standard is about the page layout (a whole page split into two columns). A small side-by-side section, such as Important Links or a logo beside your intro, is fine. The audit still flags these; skip that item for now. The check is being corrected and re-run next week.</li>
<li><strong>Past dates on a page.</strong> Review the page with your team. It is often a chance to post a short update. If your team decides the wording stays, say so in the note on the item and mark it done.</li>
<li><strong>Asking for help.</strong> Use Still stuck? on the item and give as much detail as you can. Questions are answered in order, and a question several people ask moves up the list.</li>
<li><strong>Items only Finalsite can fix</strong> (template markup and some PDF rules) should not be on your list. They are being filtered out again.</li>
</ul>
' || '<p>The most common red item so far is <strong>Quick Access buttons</strong>'),
 '<details class="doc-accordion nested"><summary>Department Widgets</summary>', '<details class="doc-accordion nested"><summary>Tell Your Department''s Story</summary><div class="section-block">
<p>The District is shifting from making sure department websites are correct to helping departments tell their story, the same way schools are asked to. Stories will come from the work your department is doing: videos, spotlights and updates that show how your department supports the District''s mission.</p>
<p><strong>Start with an editorial calendar.</strong> List the events and moments your department has every year in a simple spreadsheet. Then plan a few campaigns ahead of time, and reuse content from last year where it still fits. Content made with reuse in mind can run year after year until something major changes.</p>
<p>More guidance and best practices are coming, including at the next quarterly meeting (along with a video production pilot and a tool to scan and fix PDFs without Acrobat). The one-on-one sessions are where we help you plan it.</p>
</div></details>' || '<details class="doc-accordion nested"><summary>Department Widgets</summary>'),
 'What''s Changed</summary>
<div class="body">', 'What''s Changed</summary>
<div class="body">' || '<h2>October 29, 2026</h2><p>Status updated to 45 certified, with the course open through the weekend and the check at the end of the day Monday, November 2. From the October 29 Hot Lab: check that your audit lists only your pages, side-by-side sections are allowed, what to do with past dates, how to ask for help, and Finalsite-only items. Added Tell Your Department''s Story.</p>'),
 'One Hot Lab is left before the deadline: Thursday, October 29.', 'Next Hot Lab: Tuesday, November 3.')
where slug='wcm-department' and brand_slug='bcps' and content not like '%Tell Your Department''s Story%';
update public.briefings set updated_at=now(), content =
 replace(replace(replace(replace(regexp_replace(content, '<p><strong>Status\.</strong>.*?</p>', '<p><strong>Status.</strong> Certification is due <strong>Friday, October 30, 2026</strong>, and 45 department WCMs have completed it. The course stays open through the weekend. <strong>At the end of the day Monday, November 2, we check who has not finished, and a WCM who has not finished loses access to edit your department pages until they complete it.</strong> WCMs who are close get a personal follow-up. If someone new has taken over your department''s pages, as happened in Emergency Management this week, tell us and we will fast-track them through certification so the work is not held up. Two things help most this week: check in with your WCM on where they are in the course, and confirm your Web Content Manager if you have not yet.</p>'),
 '<span class="meta-label">Last Updated</span><span class="meta-value">October 28, 2026</span>', '<span class="meta-label">Last Updated</span><span class="meta-value">October 29, 2026</span>'),
 'so treat today''s score as a to-do list rather than a grade.</p>', 'so treat today''s score as a to-do list rather than a grade.</p>' || '<p><strong>Updated October 29.</strong> Each department''s audit now lists only that department''s pages. Some departments include functions with their own Web Content Manager (for example Emergency Management within Safety, Security and Emergency Preparedness, or EEO / ADA Compliance within Labor Relations), and from the outside they can look like one office. Your WCM is checking that their list is right; if your department has functions managed by different people, letting us know who manages which pages is the fastest fix.</p>
<p><strong>Telling your department''s story.</strong> The work is shifting from making sure your website is correct to helping your department tell its story: videos, spotlights and updates about how your department supports the District''s mission. A simple editorial calendar of the events your department has every year is a good start, and the one-on-one sessions with the District Web Team are where we help plan it.</p>
'),
 'What''s Changed</h3></summary>
<div class="section-block">
', 'What''s Changed</h3></summary>
<div class="section-block">
' || '<p><span class="change-date">October 29, 2026.</span> Status updated to 45 certified, the course open through the weekend and the check on Monday, November 2, and fast-tracking new WCMs. Added that audits list only your department''s pages and that departments with functions managed by different people should tell us who manages which pages. Added telling your department''s story.</p>
'),
 'One Hot Lab is left before the deadline, Thursday, October 29, and anyone stuck on a module can bring it there.', 'The next Hot Lab is Tuesday, November 3.')
where slug='director-department' and brand_slug='bcps' and content not like '%Updated October 29.%';

